{"kind":"request","text":"Roles, flow and instances, slice RI1 (notes/2026-10-21-roles-flow-and-instances.md on main 184ba58d, section 10): enrol a further key for an existing agent or checker member.\n\nToday no tool issues `invite-key` for an existing agent member. `dap invite --kind agent-key` always adds a new member first (packages/cli/src/invitations.ts:269-270), and hosted MCP `create` makes a new member each time (packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts:213-256). Membership already allows several active keys for one member (packages/platform/src/membership.ts:360-414).\n\nWork:\n1. CLI: `dap invite --kind agent-key --member @handle` signs only `invite-key` for the existing member, with kind `agent` or `checker`, and prints the link. `dap join` with that link enrols the new key for the same member (enrolAgentKey, invitations.ts:307-430, accepts an invitation with no add-member).\n2. Hosted MCP: a control request enrols a further key for an existing member, under the same authority checks as `create` (docs/mcp.md, \"Creating an agent: the controller's recipe\"). It returns a new bearer for the new key only.\n3. docs/mcp.md and docs/cli.md: the recipe for a second and third instance of one identity, and how to retire one instance's key with `revoke-key`.\n\nDone when: a member with three active keys acts with each one; each entry's observation names its key; retiring one key leaves the member and the other two keys working; a second link for the same slot is refused, and a repeated control request with the same `op` answers the same.\n\nOrder: a small slice. It runs after the retained-files slices RF1 to RF4 and beside the 6dd06d03 security requests 5 to 10. The archive slices keep priority when one is ready. Checker review of the exact head. No deployment by the builder. RI2 to RI4 follow the Counter contracts revision 4, which the planner writes next.","body":{"conditions":"CLI and hosted MCP enrol a further key for an existing agent or checker member; docs recipes; three